  "body": "### Describe the bug\n\nWe use Jumpcloud as an OIDC authentication provider, and connect only one group per user for OIDC authentication. In this case, the list of groups is sent as a string (just the one group name), not an array. Homarr seems to expect an array, and group assignment is not working in such case.\n\nIn the debug output we see (abbreviated):\nE.g. with single group - group assignment not working:\n```\n  \"email\": \"test.user@example.com\",\n  \"groups\": \"homarr-user-group\",\n```\n\nE.g. with multiple groups - group assignment working:\n```\n  \"email\": \"test.user@example.com\",\n  \"groups\": [\n    \"homarr-user-group\",\n    \"homarr-dummy-group\"\n  ],\n```\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n* Configure Homarr OAuth with a provider that sends a sinlge OAuth groups as a string instead of an array\n* Create group with same name in Homarr\n* Map permissions to that group\n* Log in with user mapped to that single group\n* Observe user being created, but not mapped to that group in Homarr\n\n### Impact\n\nImpact: medium I'd say - it's a bit tedious to debug because it's not obvious what's going on, and only from the debug logs one might be able to deduce the correlation of the single group not being in an array might cause the group mapping problem\n\nWorkaround: ensure to always send at least two groups\n\n### Additional information\n\nI found a similar bug in the harbor registry (https://goharbor.io/) that led me to figure out this issue.\n* https://github.com/goharbor/harbor/issues/15416\n\n### Version\n\n1.61.0\n\n### Installation method\n\nHelm\n\n### Browser\n\nFirefox",
